Z||000000||87ECO5||06-01-2001||12:44 PM||||My company just upgraded my PC to Windows 2000 and, when I attempted to reinstall my MP3 player, it told me <B>I must have Administrative Authority to perform this function</B>!!!<P>So, I'm resorting to using the standard Windows Media Player.<P>Now, my problem - does anyone know how to create playlists for WMP?  With my other MP3 player (MusicMatch), I was able to load a playlist and have hours of uninterrupted music.  I hate the idea of having to click on each individual song.<P>HELP!!!!!<P>TIA||||reg||5
Z||000001||Jaygee79||06-01-2001||12:59 PM||||If you click on Media Library you can create playlists in there.<P>------------------<BR>Jaime<BR>84SE red<BR>AOL IM: Jaygee79<BR><A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/jaygee79/index.html" TARGET=_blank>Jaygee79's Web Page</A><BR>     <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/pooheey1.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000002||87ECO5||06-01-2001||01:41 PM|||| <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/confused.gif">   Hmmmm ... when I use the player's help feature, I can't find anything about the library.<P>Am I looking in the wrong place?  BTW, in case it makes a difference, the version I have is 6.4.09.1109.||||reg||5
Z||000003||Jaygee79||06-01-2001||01:58 PM||||You need the newer version.  The older one doesn't have playlists.  Go to the microsoft site and download the new one.  It takes more memory but it has more features.<P>------------------<BR>Jaime<BR>84SE red<BR>AOL IM: Jaygee79<BR><A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/jaygee79/index.html" TARGET=_blank>Jaygee79's Web Page</A><BR>      <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/pooheey1.jpg">  <p>[This message has been edited by Jaygee79 (edited 06-01-2001).]||||reg||1
