Z||000005||theogre||06-01-2001||02:22 PM||||Win2K is just another upgrade of WinNT. You MUST be a "local administrator" on the box to install software. One of the reasons your employer put in Win2k was to prevent people doing exactly what you are trying to do. Inotherwords... They don't want unapproved software on the machine. Very few people in the company are likely to be given local admin on the machines.<P>If you work for First USA or Banc One out there I can tell you that getting local admin rights is about as likely as pigs flying.... It ain't happenin.||||reg||1
Z||000006||87ECO5||06-01-2001||02:54 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by theogre:<BR><B>Very few people in the company are likely to be given local admin on the machines.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>... unless you have a buddy in the PC desktop department!!!!!    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>I was just given local admin to my machine.  Of course, it'll probably be taken away once the higher-ups find out.<P>So, I best get started on my installs!!!!!    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||14
